<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<!-- Texto voltado pro público (Reino Unido) — inglês britânico de propósito (honour, organise, etc.), não americano. -->
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Privacy Policy — {{ site_title }}</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ site_url }}/privacy.html">
<style>
  :root {
    color-scheme: light dark;
    --bg: #0b0d12; --surface: #151822; --text: #eef0f4; --text-muted: #9aa1b2;
    --accent: #ff5f6d; --border: #262b3a;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
    :root { --bg: #f5f6f8; --surface: #ffffff; --text: #14161c; --text-muted: #5c6270; --border: #e4e6eb; }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); }
  main { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
  .updated { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  .back-link { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  address { font-style: normal; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <a class="back-link" href="index.html">← Back to {{ site_title }}</a>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: {{ updated_at }}</p>

  <p>
    This policy explains how {{ controller_name }} ("we", "us") collects and uses your personal
    data when you subscribe to our daily deals email newsletter, in line with the UK GDPR and the
    Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR). See also our
    <a href="terms.html">Terms of Use</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <address>
    {{ controller_name }}<br>
    {{ address_line1 }}, {{ address_city }}, {{ address_postal_code }}, {{ address_country }}<br>
    Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ controller_email }}">{{ controller_email }}</a>
  </address>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you subscribe through our signup form, we collect: your email address, the timestamp of
    your consent, and confirmation that you actively checked the consent box. We do not collect
    any other personal information, and this site does not use tracking or analytics cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>
    We use your email address solely to send you our daily deals newsletter, which you explicitly
    opted into. The legal basis for this processing is your consent (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(a)),
    which you can withdraw at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Double opt-in</h2>
  <p>
    After submitting the signup form, you'll receive a confirmation email. You are only added to
    our mailing list once you click the confirmation link — submitting the form alone does not
    subscribe you.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    We use <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brevo</a>
    as our email service provider to store your contact details and send the newsletter on our
    behalf. Brevo processes this data as our data processor, under its own privacy policy and
    security safeguards. We do not sell or share your email address with any other third party.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your email address for as long as you remain subscribed. If you unsubscribe, we keep a
    minimal record (email address and the date you unsubscribed) for a reasonable period to honour
    your opt-out and for our own compliance record-keeping, after which it is deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK GDPR you have the right to access, correct, or delete your personal data, to restrict
    or object to its processing, and to receive a copy of it in a portable format. To exercise any
    of these rights, or to unsubscribe, email us at
    <a href="mailto:{{ controller_email }}">{{ controller_email }}</a> or use the unsubscribe link
    included in every newsletter email. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time; the date above reflects the latest revision.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
